      ],
      "text" : "6 2 √ Our Solution."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960100000000011,
        695.97924480000006,
        425.15533077647353,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "The previous example could have been done in fewer steps if we had noticed that"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960100000000011,
        672.74280799999997,
        425.2010503260928,
        20.455347200000006
      ],
      "text" : "72= 36· 2, but often the time it takes to discover the larger perfect square is more"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.961000000000013,
        666.57924479999997,
        238.81345459159041,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "than it would take to simplify in several steps."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.961000000000013,
        640.29914480000002,
        425.25582291159037,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "Variables often are part of the radicand as well. When taking the square roots of"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.961000000000013,
        623.37924480000004,
        303.85313171146242,
        13.178337699999929
      ],
      "text" : "variables, we can divide the exponent by 2. For example,"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        393.84082000000006,
        623.37924480000004,
        116.32040986470389,
        22.767155200000047
      ],
      "text" : "√ = x4, because we"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        403.80100000000004,
        623.37924480000004,
        10.952048409999975,
        13.178337699999929
      ],
      "text" : "x8"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960219999999936,
        608.61904479999998,
        425.25372882122235,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "divide the exponent of 8 by 2. This follows from the power of a power rule of"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960219999999936,
        593.97924479999995,
        83.552068409999976,
        13.298257699999908
      ],
      "text" : "expoennts, (x4)2"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 7.9701100000000009,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        171.36023999999992,
        593.97924479999995,
        338.78602209515526,
        13.298257699999908
      ],
      "text" : "= x8. When squaring, we multiply the exponent by two, so when"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960159999999902,
        579.3390447999999,
        425.12487317248002,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "taking a square root we divide the exponent by 2. This is shown in the following"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960159999999917,
        564.57924479999986,
        45.371846978815995,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "example."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.960159999999917,
        520.79119999999989,
        79.690012213629473,
        11.955199999999991
      ],
      "text" : "Example 381."
    },
